12|0@JRPG^1438910677#ctub06s:scaryisntit$:No. But the 'fans' will say SquareEnix have anyway. People are going to heavily criticise FFVII's remake. There is no escaping this. There are people who want the same exact game as the original, just with better graphics. There are people who want something different from the combat system and the story. One or both of these will rip the game to shreds. Even if the remake was just a remake with nothing revamped, the littlest changes would be nitpicked simply because of the ludicrously high level of nostalgia on the game. Frankly, I'm surprised SquareEnix actually went ahead with the remake. I would not have blamed them if they never did simply because the chances of not having a vocal minority (as they always are) kick up the biggest stink they'll ever see are extremely low (in my opinion). FFXV... too many posters on reddit are far too into the circlejerk about 'this game has been in development since 2006' (again, probably a vocal minority but Jesus I see this in almost every topic). Which isn't true. Versus was cancelled. The idea for that game didn't pan out to a working game. End of story. XV is a different game from around 2011 or 2012 involving action combat and a few ideas from Versus and FNC mythology. You can already see a ton of criticism toward the combat. 'It's not FF anymore' I have read more times than I care to, simply because the combat isn't turn based. Some are expecting the world because of that '10 years in development' obsession. I have no doubt that FFXV will be a good game. But the expectations based on that absurd 'it's been in development for 10 years' obsession of certain individuals will be a factor the game being torn apart. I am very pessimistic, as you can see, about both of these games. SquareEnix receives a lot of hate on reddit. I have little faith that a quality game will stop the vehemence. Either VII's remake or XV, they'll be torn apart by a vocal group on reddit either way. God how I hope I am wrong.
